Placement - Rate Limiter should be placed inside the API gateway

Functional Requirements -
Rate limiter should limit the number of request from a certain user within a certain period of time to avoid spam. This is done to reduce the load on the load balancer. This user can be banned from submitting requests for a certain period of time or forever based on data.
Rate limiter should limit the number of requests [overall] sent to the load balancer as per load balancer's maximum capacity or 90% of maximum capacity.
Rate limiter should be logging every request for tracking purposes so analysis can be drawn and actions can be taken based on the data. This can include requests per customer/per api end point/per region/requests at different times of the day.
Rate limiter should be asynchronously saving the logs in a designated area in case the rate limiter goes down, we have the data upto that point.
